WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.000
<v Alex>Welcome everyone. Let's go through the kick-off slides.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.000
<v Alex>We're aiming to ship Phase 1 by end of next week.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
<v Bo>Two of us full time should be enough if scope holds.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Alex>On to the architecture. It's a single-process CLI.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Alex>Cache is keyed by URL hash, same convention as today.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Cam>The block diagram on the next slide is the same one from the design doc.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.000
<v Alex>Open question: what retention do we want for generated notes?

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.000
<v Bo>I'd say keep them indefinitely. Frames can be purged on the existing schedule.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.000
<v Cam>Agreed. We can make it configurable.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.000
<v Alex>Last slide. Alex writes the spec, Bo prototypes the parser, Cam reviews end of week.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.000
<v Bo>Sounds good.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.000
<v Cam>Works for me.
